      "text": "When the ball is dropped from a height of $243$ cm, the height after the first bounce is $\\frac{2}{3} \\times 243 = 162$ cm. The height after the second bounce is $\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\times 162 = 108$ cm. The height after the third bounce is $\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\times 108 = 72$ cm. The height after the fourth bounce is $\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\times 72 = 48$ cm. The height after the fifth bounce is $\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\times 48 = 32$ cm. The height after the sixth bounce is $\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\times 32 = \\frac{64}{3} \\approx 21.33$ cm. Therefore, the ball first rises to less than $30$ cm after the fourth bounce. The answer is $\\boxed{4}$.",
