      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's denote the height from which the ball is dropped as \\( h_0 = 243 \\) cm. Each time the ball bounces, it reaches a height that is \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the height from which it fell. Therefore, the height after each bounce can be described by the following sequence:\n\n1. After the first bounce: \\( h_1 = 243 \\times \\frac{2}{3} \\)\n2. After the second bounce: \\( h_2 = h_1 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 243 \\times \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 \\)\n3. After the third bounce: \\( h_3 = h_2 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 243 \\times \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^3 \\)\n4. And so on...\n\nWe can generalize the height after \\( n \\) bounces as:\n\\[ h_n = 243 \\times \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n \\]\n\nWe need to find the smallest integer \\( n \\) such that \\( h_n < 30 \\) cm. Therefore, we set up the inequality:\n\\[ 243 \\times \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n < 30 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( n \\), we first isolate \\(\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n\\) by dividing both sides by 243:\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n < \\frac{30}{243} \\]\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n < \\frac{10}{81} \\]\n\nNext, we take the natural logarithm of both sides to solve for \\( n \\):\n\\[ \\ln\\left(\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n\\right) < \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right) \\]\n\\[ n \\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) < \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right) \\]\n\nSince \\(\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\) is negative, we divide both sides by \\(\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\) and reverse the inequality:\n\\[ n > \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)} \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the values of the logarithms:\n\\[ \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right) = \\ln(10) - \\ln(81) \\approx 2.3026 - 4.3945 = -2.0919 \\]\n\\[ \\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\approx -0.4055 \\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the inequality, we get:\n\\[ n > \\frac{-2.0919}{-0.4055} \\approx 5.15 \\]\n\nSince \\( n \\) must be an integer, we round up to the next whole number:\n\\[ n = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the ball first rises to a height less than 30 cm after \\(\\boxed{6}\\) bounces.",
